Switchcraft R5 validation (2026-11-13)

Switchcraft source: 1d716dbe17f9870e5c2cfbeb351d839ea91412fb
java-switch runtime pin: a0f0e168bb282e9585c0353c3d9b70a7ad043ce8
SD ZIP SHA-256: 008b93e3af2cbb26ed3069f4d5ad336f2721f30256a972ad517a8aa96c0a5a98

R4 PHYSICAL: zero-services opens and its L eager C-heap memory contract passes.
The genuine VM reaches vm-ready, but Hello, application JNI/FFM and agent
classes are missing. Graphics, audio, shader and Minecraft workloads are NOT
REACHED. The 21 raw logs and their byte-preserved hashes are in the source.

R5 FIXES: local file-URL translation for JAR/directory classes and resources,
fresh standalone diagnostic source stamps, explicit complete menu redraw/flush.
SDK ABI 1 and one VM per application process remain unchanged.

R5 HORIZON: NOT TESTED. Start with one fresh standalone java25-test A. Actual
Hello output and stage completed are required before dependent Java workloads.
No Minecraft title on Switch is claimed.

HOST: all 92 Switchcraft tests passed, including the official client renderer
transform and actual SDL/Vulkan/VMA 60-frame test with Khronos validation
enabled on Mesa llvmpipe. All 23 runtime tests and the class-library suite pass.
Maintained patched JDK loaders reproduce the unpatched CNFE, then load real
JAR/directory classes and resource streams. The supplemental fresh sole-localhost
URL loader check passes. These results are HOST ONLY.

BUILD: the genuine instrumented OpenJDK25 Zero Minecraft profile cross-built,
including the complete ten-module classfile-69 image and real native JDK
providers. Clean source/package reconstruction verification passed. All four
standalone diagnostics were relinked at the clean final runtime SHA, and actual
ELF/NRO identity and SD-copy hashes were audited. The combined final link has
zero undefined symbols and no GL/EGL API definitions. Final NRO formats, SD
inventory/hashes, matching source/debug/SDK companions and ZIP checks pass.

REPRODUCTION:
Build java-switch at the immutable pin using:
  bash scripts/build-openjdk25-runtime.sh --with-instrument --with-minecraft
Then build Switchcraft at its immutable source using:
  JAVA_SWITCH_SOURCE=/path/to/java-switch bash scripts/build-all.sh
For this complete host run the following environment was also used:
  SWITCHCRAFT_CLIENT_JAR=/tmp/r4-mc-reference/client.jar
  SWITCHCRAFT_SHADER_BUILD_DIR=/tmp/switchcraft-shader-build
  SWITCHCRAFT_GRAPHICS_HOST_RUN=1 DISPLAY=:93 SDL_VIDEODRIVER=x11
  XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/tmp
  VK_ICD_FILENAMES=/tmp/r4-mc-reference/debian-mesa/root/usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/lvp_icd.json
  VK_LAYER_PATH=/tmp/switchcraft-validation-layer/usr/share/vulkan/explicit_layer.d
  VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS=VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation
  LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/tmp/r4-mc-reference/debian-mesa/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu:/tmp/switchcraft-validation-layer/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu

These /tmp paths are local research caches. Game assets, desktop JDKs/natives,
credentials and keys are excluded from the SD ZIP and source companion. The
historical 2026-11-12 official snapshot Demo title screenshot is HOST ONLY;
that title run was not repeated for this Horizon path-conversion change.


